  "body": "After PR #881, the renderer's claim route changes visible state, but still runs with `$changesData = false`, so nothing signals the change.\n\n## Where\n\n- `controllers/Api/LabelRenderApiController.php` (~:39): the `labels-render-claim` route's `InRequestTransaction(..., false)`\n- `services/Labels/RenderRequestService.php`: `Claim()` (settles invalid requests, expires previews, dead-letters waiting print jobs)\n\n## Evidence\n\nSince #881, one claim tick can mark render requests `invalid` or `failed`/`expired`, dead-letter print jobs, and collect expired previews. `MarkDbChanged` is not called for any of these.\n\n## Failure scenario\n\nA monitor or page that refreshes on the data-changed signal keeps showing print jobs as waiting, and render requests as pending, until something unrelated changes data.\n\n## Possible direction\n\nPass `true` when the claim tick changed anything, or call `MarkDbChanged` from the settle, expire and dead-letter paths.\n\n## How this was found\n\nReported by an independent validator during the 2026-10-12 audit remediation (issues #846–#868), while it reviewed PR #881 (#846, #857, #858). Depends on #881 being merged.\n",
